      "description": "Watch PEC Zwolle vs Ajax highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The PEC Zwolle vs Ajax clash at the MAC³PARK Stadion promised high intensity and tactical intrigue in this Eredivisie fixture. Both sides looked to establish their rhythm early on in a match where discipline would ultimately play a decisive role. First Half Stalemate The match, played on August 9, 2026 , began with Ajax dominating possession but struggling to break down a compact PEC Zwolle defense. Caio Henrique was active on the wings, delivering multiple corners that failed to find a teammate. PEC Zwolle had their moments, notably when Tobias Sommer directed a header towards goal, but Marc-Andre ter Stegen was well-positioned to make a comfortable save. The first half ended goalless, characterized by tactical fouling and a yellow card for Abdellah Ouazane . The Red Card Turning Point The complexion of the game changed dramatically in the 57th minute. Sherel Floranus was shown a straight red card, leaving PEC Zwolle a man down and sparking heavy protests from the home side. Sensing an opportunity, the Ajax manager made a series of attacking substitutions, bringing on Jorthy Mokio , Mika Godts , and Julian Brandt . The pressure mounted as the visitors began to exploit the extra space on the pitch, forcing the hosts into a deep defensive shell. Late Goals Decide the Contest The breakthrough finally arrived in the 76th minute. After a period of sustained pressure, Tolu Arokodare and Lucas Rosa combined to set up Jorthy Mokio , who finished clinically with his left foot to give Ajax the lead. PEC Zwolle tried to respond through tactical shifts, but their frustration boiled over as Gabriel Reiziger and Koen Kostons both received yellow cards in the closing stages. With the hosts pushing forward, Ajax struck again in the 95th minute; Mika Godts provided a precise assist for Julian Brandt , who made no mistake with his right foot to seal the 0-2 victory."
